\description{
Build mzLib's observation table from a stored FlashLFQ or MetaMorpheus peptide table: every peptide in every biological sample as log2 intensity or no value with the reason, with the shared-peptide normalization shifts, and optionally the peptide-by-sample table stats fit reads.

mzLib's \code{FlashLfqObservations.FromPeptideTable} reads a stored FlashLFQ or MetaMorpheus peptide
table, maps each run's detection type to a state, sums each technical replicate's fractions on the
linear scale and averages a sample's replicates in log2. Then \code{SharedPeptideNormalization.Measure}
measures how far each sample sits from the others on the peptides they share; \code{normalize = TRUE}
subtracts it.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_observations}:

  - \code{records}, a data.frame with one row per (peptide, sample), peptides ordinal by full
    sequence: \code{full_sequence}, the engine's modified sequence, the key; \code{base_sequence};
    \code{protein_groups}, a list column of every group the peptide table names (\code{UNDEFINED} = in no
    surviving group); \code{unique_protein_group}, the one group it is unique to, \code{NA} when shared,
    \code{UNDEFINED} or none; \code{sample}; \code{log2_intensity} (log2 of FlashLFQ intensity units), fractions
    summed, replicates averaged in log2, less the shift with \code{normalize = TRUE}, and \code{NA} for
    \strong{no value} (see \code{state}), never 0; and \code{state}, one of \code{"quantified"}, \code{"mbr_transferred"},
    \code{"ambiguous_peak"}, \code{"identified_not_quantified"} or \code{"not_detected"}. Empty with \code{out}.
  - \code{peptides_file}, \code{protein_groups_file} and \code{samples_file} as absolute paths, the last two
    \code{NA} when not given; \code{basis} and \code{normalize} as given; \code{min_peptides} (peptides) as given, \code{NA}
    when mzLib's floor applied; \code{run_count} runs; \code{runs}, a data.frame of the runs as mzLib holds
    them (\code{file_name}, \code{sample_id}, \code{fraction}, \code{technical_replicate}), ordinal by file name;
    \code{sample_count} samples; \code{samples}; \code{samples_without_values}; \code{peptide_count} peptides;
    \code{protein_group_count} protein groups; \code{protein_groups}, a data.frame of those groups (\code{name},
    \code{q_value} a fraction 0 to 1 or \code{NA} if not finite, \code{is_decoy}, \code{is_contaminant},
    \code{is_entrapment}, \code{genes} or \code{NA}); \code{state_counts}, rows (cells) per state; \code{warnings};
    \code{written} (\code{path}, \code{format}, \code{row_count}) or \code{NULL}; \code{responses_written} (\code{path}, \code{format},
    \code{row_count} peptides, \code{sample_count} samples) or \code{NULL}; \code{row_count} rows, \code{peptide_count} x
    \code{sample_count}; \code{column_names}.
  - \code{normalization}, mzLib's \code{NormalizationResult}, measured whether or not it was applied:
    \code{setting}, \code{"shared_peptide_median"} (the peptides with a value in every sample),
    \code{"shared_peptide_median_half"} (in at least half; used when too few are in all) or \code{"none"}
    (too few either way: no sample shifted); \code{reference_set_size} (peptides) in the set used;
    \code{minimum_reference_set_size} (peptides), the floor used; \code{shifts}, each sample's shift in log2
    units, \code{NA} for a sample with no shift; and \code{warnings}.
  - \code{caveats}: how values are combined, what the basis does, what mzLib cannot check about the
    table, and what the normalization assumes.

}
\section{The traps}{


Median normalization assumes most peptides do not change between samples. When most of them do -
a table of the spiked organism alone, a loading series, a pull-down - normalizing deletes the
result: read \code{normalization$shifts} before you subtract them. The peptide table does not record
the design FlashLFQ quantified with, so give the runs that design. mzLib does not yet roll
peptides up to proteins or choose a test's rows, so neither does this.

}
