\item{\code{mzlib_usage_error} (usage)}{mzLib refuses the input (its ArgumentException, reclassified): two runs with one file name or one place (sample, replicate, fraction); a table column no run matches, or a run no column matches; IsoTracker output; a blank, negative or non-finite intensity or an unreadable detection type; a peptide listed twice; a group name holding ';'; a \code{--samples} id the table does not have}
\item{\code{mzlib_bridge_error} (correctness)}{never expected}
\item{\code{mzlib_service_unavailable} (service_unavailable)}{Never raised by this verb.}
}
}
\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item A missing value is null, never 0, and state says why. Fractions of one technical replicate are summed on the linear scale, then a sample's technical replicates are averaged on the log2 scale (mzLib's ObservationTable).
\item Under msms_only a match-between-runs value enters no sum, but its cell still says mbr_transferred; under mbr_kept it enters, and the cell says mbr_transferred.
\item The peptide table does not record the design FlashLFQ quantified with, so mzLib cannot check that these runs group the files as FlashLFQ did. FlashLFQ withholds every fraction of a sample whose strongest fraction is ambiguous; give the runs the design it quantified with, or a value it withheld can become a partial sum.
\item FlashLFQ writes its peptide table in the culture of the machine it ran on and mzLib reads it as invariant (a decimal point), so a table written where the decimal separator is a comma does not read correctly.
\item Every peptide is a row: decoy, contaminant and entrapment peptides, and peptides of groups at any q-value, included. mzLib does not yet choose the rows a differential test uses, or roll peptides up to proteins, so \code{--responses-out} is peptide by sample only. Filter rows with protein_groups and unique_protein_group.
\item The normalization shifts are always measured (SharedPeptideNormalization.Measure) over every sample of the table, after \code{--samples}; they are subtracted only with \code{--normalize}. Measure one stratum at a time. A sample whose shift is null is not shifted.
}
}
